SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Implemented the Ingest X-Ray surface as an adaptive SwiftUI page (macOS regular /
iPad regular / iPhone compact, ADR-002/006), driven by a single @Observable
IngestXRayPageModel over a KMP-style data-source seam (ADR-004 — zero networking
in the view). Reproduces the full web page: the title/subtitle chrome (web
PageContainer) and its four GlassPanels — the controls bar (GlassPanel1: vehicle /
window / bucket pickers, with the bucket menu auto-disabling any bucket that is not
strictly finer than the window, web `tooBig`), the no-vehicle empty prompt
(GlassPanel2), the bucketed sample-count bar chart (GlassPanel3, native Swift Charts
— never a WKWebView), and the sortable per-field statistics table (GlassPanel4).
Between the controls and the report panels it renders the web XRayHeader summary
strip (three stat tiles). Each report panel switches its own data state
(loading / empty / error / success) in place rather than gating the surface.

The page reuses the shared P3 Ingest-X-Ray pure cores already in the module
(TeslaSync/feature-views/XRay*) for byte-identical logic — the value types
(IngestXRayWindow/Bucket, XRayFieldStat, XRayBucketInput, XRayVehicleRef,
IngestXRaySummary), the projections (XRayHeaderProjection.fmtInt,
XRayControlsProjection.isBucketDisabled, XRayFieldsProjector, XRayBucketChartProjection,
XRayValueKind), and the sort transition (XRayFieldsModel.nextSort) — while rendering
every visible string from the central Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names
(the standalone P3 component VIEWS pull from per-surface tables, so they are NOT
reused — the page owns its chrome like the sibling DLQInspectorPage). SI N/A: ingest
counts are exact integers and window/bucket are control-plane selections; timestamps
format at the display boundary. Ingest X-Ray is a polled REST query (web INTERVALS.FAST),
not an SSE source, so no live SSE subscription applies (ADR-013 staleness N/A).

